1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,682
Movies show bullets

2
00:00:00,691 --> 00:00:02,242
chasing swimmers
underwater. Instead,

3
00:00:02,303 --> 00:00:02,786
bullets stop

4
00:00:02,795 --> 00:00:03,308
at three feet.

5
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:04,015
The moment

6
00:00:04,026 --> 00:00:04,983
it leaves the barrel

7
00:00:04,995 --> 00:00:06,126
and slams into water,

8
00:00:06,196 --> 00:00:06,838
it hits a wall

9
00:00:06,943 --> 00:00:07,771
eight hundred times

10
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:08,637
denser than air.

11
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:09,647
Out front,

12
00:00:09,731 --> 00:00:10,933
extreme pressure boils

13
00:00:10,945 --> 00:00:11,906
the water instantly,

14
00:00:11,991 --> 00:00:12,748
wrapping the spinning

15
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,529
nose inside

16
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:14,634
a silver gas bubble.

17
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:16,208
But that speed
backfires,

18
00:00:16,228 --> 00:00:17,624
the bubble
collapses sideways,

19
00:00:17,676 --> 00:00:18,958
violently twisting
the bullet

20
00:00:18,979 --> 00:00:19,620
until it shreds

21
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:20,630
into tiny shards.

22
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:21,927
So firing faster

23
00:00:21,936 --> 00:00:22,659
actually
makes it stop

24
00:00:22,668 --> 00:00:23,657
sooner. Meanwhile,

25
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:24,219
a slower heavy

26
00:00:24,228 --> 00:00:24,996
round glides straight

27
00:00:25,005 --> 00:00:25,664
past three feet.

28
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:26,959
Dive just three feet

29
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:27,567
under the surface,

30
00:00:27,586 --> 00:00:28,336
and a deadly rifle

31
00:00:28,346 --> 00:00:29,210
turns into harmless

32
00:00:29,219 --> 00:00:29,713
scrap metal.
